  "worked_solution": "Since $P$ is a polynomial of degree $5,$ the leading term contains an ${x}^{5}.$\n\nSince $Q$ is a polynomial of degree $9,$ the leading term contains an ${x}^{9}.$\n\nIn $P-Q,$ the highest-order term still contains an ${x}^{9}.$ No ${x}^{9}$ term in $P$ could possibly cancel out the ${x}^{9}$ term in $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the degree of $P-Q$ must be $9.$",
